From dc23773de85410bf058700e640ff1763bd4344e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Highlander Paiva <highlander.paiva@rdstation.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 11:50:13 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] Ubuntu port: package backend with vendor sources for
 what apt lacks

The Install menu failed for every package that was not installed yet:
omarchy-pkg-add looked for "Candidate:" in apt-cache's output, which is
translated under a pt_BR locale. Past that, a third of the menu named
packages apt does not carry (AUR and Omarchy's own repository), and
omarchy-pkg-aur-add still called yay.

omarchy-pkg-ubuntu resolves an Arch name under LC_ALL=C to, in order:
an apt alias (php-cli, libyaml-dev, freerdp3-x11, python3-gpg...), or a
recipe: the vendor's apt pool (Grok Bot, ChatGPT, Perplexity, Edge, whose
.debs register their own sources), a vendor apt repository (Brave, Signal,
Sublime Text, NordVPN), a vendor .deb (LM Studio, Bitwarden, Minecraft,
Heroic, Sunshine, umu-launcher), the package from pkgs.omarchy.org
extracted with a manifest and its sha256 checked (ONCE, omazed,
omarchy-emacs, T3 Code, OpenClaw, Hermes Desktop with node-pty rebuilt
for noble's glibc, xpadneo through dkms), a flatpak (Moonlight), mise
(Helix, Bitwarden CLI, Symfony CLI), Nerd Fonts release archives,
i386 multiarch (Steam, lib32 Vulkan/NVIDIA), libretro buildbot cores and
assets at Arch's paths, Zed's installer and Zen's tarball in /opt.

omarchy-pkg-installed/add/drop and omarchy-pkg-aur-add go through it,
omarchy-install-and-launch takes the flatpak id as the desktop id, and
the AUR entry is hidden when yay is absent.
